        "text": "No numerical September Canadian pump-price observation was accessible in this run. The US increase is an auxiliary regional fuel signal, excluded from the Canadian headline history and dispersion calculation. I assume a smaller 5.0% Canadian gasoline monthly increase. That is a forecast assumption, not a fetched Canadian statistic. Broad non-energy momentum receives zero net adjustment; travel seasonality and the elevated year-earlier travel comparison receive a judgmental -0.10 percentage-point adjustment. Continuing the existing excise suspension contributes zero incremental September policy adjustment."
