        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Model: headline-rate persistence with index-base, fuel-proxy and seasonal updates. Historical sample: six March-August 2026 official NSA annual prints [2.4, 2.8, 3.2, 2.8, 3.0, 3.0]. Updates: -0.0285 percentage points for the comparison index, +0.2065 for assumed fuel pressure, -0.10 for seasonal travel, zero broad non-energy momentum and zero incremental tax effect. Successive changes are [0.4, 0.4, -0.4, 0.2, 0.0], with mean 0.12. Their squared deviations sum to 0.448; sigma = 0.3347 percentage points, calculated as sqrt(0.448/(5-1)). A normal 80% approximation gives half-width 1.28*0.334664 = 0.42837. Around the rounded 3.1% forecast, implied bounds are 2.67163% and 3.52837%, rounded outward to 2.67% and 3.53%. No additional width multiplier is applied. This uses realized rate dispersion rather than independently calibrated forecast errors."
